rue] [17592186308191 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308192 13194139534759 true] [17592186308191 1089 "q-97159" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308191 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534759 true] [17592186308191 1100 "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,6b+c⟩$ if   \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=2+3\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,c⟩=3+8\\text{i}.$" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308191 1113 #uuid "4d2a3e3d-fac2-529b-bde6-b9bc5f4517f4" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308191 1145 "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,6b+c⟩ & =⟨a,6b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =\\overset{―}{6}⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =6⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNext, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ & =6\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+⟨a,c⟩ & =6(\\overset{―}{2+3\\text{i}})+(3+8\\text{i}) \\\\  & =6(2-3\\text{i})+(3+8\\text{i}) \\\\  & =12-18\\text{i}+3+8\\text{i} \\\\  & =15-10\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308193 13194139534759 true] [17592186308192 1