198 1113 #uuid "16657068-2558-5f9e-bf6b-f53d86050fca" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308198 1145 "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,b+(2+5\\text{i})c⟩ & =⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,(2+5\\text{i})c⟩ \\\\  & =⟨a,b⟩+(\\overset{―}{2+5\\text{i}})⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =⟨a,b⟩+(2-5\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,b⟩+(2-5\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(2-5\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨a,c⟩:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+(2-5\\text{i})⟨a,c⟩ & =\\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}}+(2-5\\text{i})\\cdot \\text{i} \\\\  & =3+\\text{i}+(2-5\\text{i})\\cdot \\text{i} \\\\  & =3+\\text{i}+2\\text{i}-5(-1) \\\\  & =8+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308200 13194139534759 true] [17592186308199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308201 13194139534759 true] [17592186308199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308202 13194139534759 true] [17592186308199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308203 13194139534759 true] [17592186308199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308204 13194139534759 true] [17592186308199 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534759 true] [1759218