55ff0e-5512-5272-a32d-49392f4f28c1" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308233 1145 "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$  $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number.\n\n- Statement II is false. To factor out a constant multiple from the second argument, we must change it to its complex conjugate.\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308235 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308236 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308237 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308238 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308239 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1041 "selection" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308236 13194139534759 true] [17592186308234 1110 #uuid "effef674-0dac-5630-a8b8-2d53c8518066" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308235 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534759 true] [17592186308235 1111 #uuid "5381d251-9885-5c9e-a699-72f24285757a" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308236 1034 "I only" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534759 true] [17592186308236 1111 #uuid "577b9a0c-91bd-56d1-af63-ec819078319d" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308237 1034 "III only" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534759 true] [17592186308237 1111 #uuid "48e0a8b7-7260-5a55-b4d8-0d92c52c3651" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308238 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534759 true] [17592186308238 1111 #uuid "845d7f5f-8b5c-5dc3-9a52-ac98c1f2061a" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308239 1034 "II only" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534759 true] [17592186308239 1111 #uuid "cc573856-49c5-5193-a781-d378667321ad" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308240 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308241 13194139534759 true] [17592186308240 1089 "q-97296" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308240 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534759 true] [17592186308240 1100 "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨a,b⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $i⟨a,b⟩=⟨a,-ib⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- There is vector $a\\in {C}^{n}$ such that  $⟨a,a⟩<0$" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308240 1113 #uuid "6174044c-c49a-50d3-8871-9332394846b1" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308240 1145 "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is false. A complex number is equal to its conjugate if and only if it is a real number. The inner product over $C$  is a complex number in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, by the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,-ib⟩=\\overset{―}{(-i)}⟨a,b⟩=i⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false.  The inner product over $C$ is positive-definite. So, for any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩\\ge 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308242 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308243 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308244 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308245 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308246 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1041 "selection" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308246 13194139534759 true] [17592186308241 1110 #uuid "49e42b05-211a-582f-9fa8-59379f469326" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308242 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308242 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534759 true] [17592186308242 1111 #uuid "4afe5cc5-6a3f-5f9c-a3fb-fa76e06d93ed" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308243 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534759 true] [17592186308243 1111 #uuid "74419b3d-b13f-57c7-9e9f-07c716d35a99" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308244 1034 "I only" 13194139534759 true] [17592186308244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534759 true] [17592186308244 1111 #uuid "b3460bc8-25ee-503c-80